A||N||7||Elenor84||Removing and installing steering wheel without removal dohicky tool?||||1||
Z||000000||Elenor84||10-03-2001||05:34 PM||||Hey guys...just bought a gt steering wheel and I want to pop it on but I don't have a steering wheel tool...is it possible to do it without one?  If not its fine because my friend has one but I just really want to get it on!<P>thx!<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
Z||000001||lowfunds||10-03-2001||05:48 PM||||There is but I would just get your friends puller. Especially, if you have tilt steering. The way I used to get them off without a puller ,is prop your legs up behind the wheel and smack the shaft with a dead blow. While you push out with your legs. But if you can get a puller get it. It is possible to damage the shaft by the above method.<p>[This message has been edited by lowfunds (edited 10-03-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||johnt671||10-03-2001||05:50 PM||||I've changed them on quite a few of my cars without a puller.  Just take the nut holding the wheel on almost all the way off and use muscle power.  Grab the top of the wheel and pull and push on it a few times then the bottom.  Keep going back and forth and you'll feel the wheel get looser.  By leaving the the bolt on the wheel won't pop off and hit you in the head.||||reg||1
Z||000003||Voytek||10-03-2001||06:20 PM||||I bought a puller for $7.00 at AutoValue.  Why not get one?  I used it several times - it's worth the money.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/voyteks_sig2.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000004||Monkeyman||10-03-2001||07:43 PM||||Autozone rents steering wheel pullers.  It ends up free.  You give them a deposit (around $15, I think), then you get that back when you bring the puller back.  <P>Use the puller and save yourself some grief.||||reg||1
Z||000005||Gerald||10-03-2001||09:47 PM||||I have a friend thats not too bright. He broke his nose taking off a wheel with out the puller........ twice.||||reg||1
Z||000006||Tigger||10-03-2001||11:41 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Gerald:<BR><B>I have a friend thats not too bright. He broke his nose taking off a wheel with out the puller........ twice.</B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>Ouch!<P>||||reg||10
Z||000007||Elenor84||10-04-2001||02:05 AM||||Whoa!  whoa! whoa!  everyone got the wrong impression here...that I'm some cheap guy that doesen't want to pay...thats all I was asking...if it could be done just as easily without one then with one...<BR>thx for your help guys...I'll borrow my friends tomorrow!<P>------------------<BR>Lance<BR>Click Image to go to site.<BR><A HREF="http://members.nbci.com/_XMCM/lancegspage/Index.html" TARGET=_blank> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/Side1.jpg"> </A>||||reg||1
